## SERVICES (Spring `@Service`)

Model on Guava's `AbstractService` and similar: clear interface contract, implementation hidden behind it, stateless where possible.

```java
// WRONG — concrete class exposed, no interface, mixed concerns
@Service
public class UserService {
  @Autowired
  UserRepository repo;

  public User getUser(Long id) {
    if (id == null) return null;
    return repo.findById(id).orElse(null);
  }
}

// RIGHT — Guava style: interface first, implementation separate
/**
 * Manages user lifecycle operations.
 *
 * <p>Implementations must be thread-safe.
 */
public interface UserService {

  /**
   * Returns the user with the given {@code id}.
   *
   * @param id the user's unique identifier; must be positive
   * @return the matching user
   * @throws IllegalArgumentException if {@code id} is not positive
   * @throws NoSuchElementException if no user with {@code id} exists
   */
  User findById(long id);

  /**
   * Creates a new user.
   *
   * @param request the creation parameters; must not be null
   * @return the created user, with its generated ID populated
   * @throws IllegalArgumentException if {@code request} fails validation
   * @throws DuplicateEmailException if the email is already registered
   */
  User create(CreateUserRequest request);
}
```

```java
/**
 * Default {@link UserService} implementation backed by {@link UserRepository}.
 */
@Service
final class DefaultUserService implements UserService {

  private final UserRepository userRepository;
  private final Clock clock;

  // Constructor injection — never field injection
  DefaultUserService(UserRepository userRepository, Clock clock) {
    this.userRepository = checkNotNull(userRepository, "userRepository");
    this.clock = checkNotNull(clock, "clock");
  }

  @Override
  public User findById(long id) {
    checkArgument(id > 0, "id must be positive: %s", id);
    return userRepository.findById(id)
        .orElseThrow(() -> new NoSuchElementException("no user with id: " + id));
  }

  @Override
  public User create(CreateUserRequest request) {
    checkNotNull(request, "request");
    // validate first, then act
    validateCreateRequest(request);
    // ...
  }

  // Private helper — package-private only if needed for testing (@VisibleForTesting)
  private void validateCreateRequest(CreateUserRequest request) {
    checkArgument(!isNullOrEmpty(request.name()), "name must not be empty");
    checkArgument(request.name().length() <= 100,
        "name too long (%s chars): %s", request.name().length(), request.name());
  }
}
```

Rules:
- Implementation class is `final` and package-private (no `public`)
- Class name: `DefaultFooService`, `SimpleFooService` — never just `FooServiceImpl`
- Constructor injection always; `@Autowired` is optional in Spring but add it for clarity
- Validate at the top of every public method
- Private helpers are `private`; only use `@VisibleForTesting` + package-private if a test needs it

