## CONTROLLERS (Spring `@RestController`)

Controllers are thin. They translate HTTP → service call → HTTP. No business logic.

```java
// WRONG — logic in controller, mixed concerns
@RestController
public class UserController {
  @Autowired
  UserRepository userRepo;

  @GetMapping("/users/{id}")
  public ResponseEntity getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
    if (id == null || id < 0) {
      return ResponseEntity.badRequest().build();
    }
    Optional<User> user = userRepo.findById(id);
    if (user.isEmpty()) return ResponseEntity.notFound().build();
    return ResponseEntity.ok(user.get());
  }
}

// RIGHT — Guava-inspired: thin, clear, delegates everything
/**
 * REST endpoints for user management.
 *
 * <p>All validation and business logic lives in {@link UserService}.
 */
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/v1/users")
final class UserController {

  private final UserService userService;

  UserController(UserService userService) {
    this.userService = checkNotNull(userService, "userService");
  }

  /**
   * Returns the user with the given {@code id}.
   *
   * @param id the user's unique identifier
   * @return 200 with the user, 404 if not found, 400 if {@code id} is invalid
   */
  @GetMapping("/{id}")
  ResponseEntity<UserResponse> findById(@PathVariable long id) {
    try {
      final User user = userService.findById(id);
      return ResponseEntity.ok(UserResponse.from(user));
    } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
      return ResponseEntity.badRequest().build();
    } catch (NoSuchElementException e) {
      return ResponseEntity.notFound().build();
    }
  }

  @PostMapping
  @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CREATED)
  UserResponse create(@RequestBody @Valid CreateUserRequest request) {
    return UserResponse.from(userService.create(request));
  }
}
```

Rules:
- `final` class, package-private
- One constructor, constructor injection, `checkNotNull` on each dependency
- Each method is short; if it grows past ~15 lines, extract a private helper or push logic to the service
- Return types are always typed: `ResponseEntity<UserResponse>`, not raw `ResponseEntity`
- Exception mapping belongs in a `@ControllerAdvice`, not scattered across controller methods

