## CUSTOM EXCEPTIONS

```java
// WRONG — too generic, no context
throw new RuntimeException("User not found");

// RIGHT — specific exception type, descriptive message, context included
/**
 * Thrown when an operation is requested on a user that does not exist.
 */
public final class UserNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {

  private final long userId;

  public UserNotFoundException(long userId) {
    super("no user with id: " + userId);
    this.userId = userId;
  }

  /** Returns the ID of the user that was not found. */
  public long userId() {
    return userId;
  }
}
```

Rules:
- One exception per failure mode — not one generic `ServiceException`
- Always include the bad value in the message
- Accessor for the structured data (so a `@ControllerAdvice` can use it)
- `public final class`, never abstract unless you're building a hierarchy
- No checked exceptions in Spring services — use unchecked

