## IMMUTABILITY AND COLLECTIONS

```java
// WRONG — mutable, leaks internals
private List<String> tags = new ArrayList<>();

public List<String> getTags() {
  return tags; // caller can mutate this!
}

// RIGHT — Guava style: defensive immutability
private final ImmutableList<String> tags;

public ImmutableList<String> tags() {
  return tags; // safe — immutable
}

// Or with Java builtins (acceptable, not Guava):
private final List<String> tags;

public List<String> tags() {
  return Collections.unmodifiableList(tags);
}
```

```java
// Building immutable collections — prefer builders or factory methods
ImmutableList<String> allowedRoles = ImmutableList.of("ADMIN", "USER", "VIEWER");

ImmutableMap<String, Integer> statusCodes = ImmutableMap.<String, Integer>builder()
    .put("OK", 200)
    .put("NOT_FOUND", 404)
    .put("SERVER_ERROR", 500)
    .buildOrThrow();

// Java 9+ factory methods are also acceptable
List<String> roles = List.of("ADMIN", "USER");
Map<String, Integer> codes = Map.of("OK", 200, "NOT_FOUND", 404);
```

