## NAMING CONVENTIONS

Follow Google Java Style exactly.

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Classes | UpperCamelCase | `UserService`, `DefaultUserService` |
| Methods | lowerCamelCase, verb-first | `findById`, `createUser`, `isActive` |
| Fields | lowerCamelCase | `userRepository`, `clock` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT`, `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS` |
| Packages | lowercase, no underscores | `com.example.myservice.user` |

Specific Guava naming patterns:
- Static factory: `of(...)`, `from(...)`, `create(...)`, `copyOf(...)`
- Boolean methods: `is...()`, `has...()`, `can...()`
- Conversion methods: `toFoo()`, `asFoo()`
- Utility class suffixes: `Utils` or `s` — Guava uses `Strings`, `Lists`, `Maps`, `MoreObjects`
- Implementation prefix: `Default`, `Simple`, `Abstract` — never `Impl` as a suffix

