## WHAT NOT TO DO

These are the most common anti-patterns. Fix them when you see them.

```java
// 1. ServiceImpl suffix — use Default, Simple, or nothing
// WRONG
class UserServiceImpl implements UserService { ... }
// RIGHT
final class DefaultUserService implements UserService { ... }

// 2. Field injection — constructor injection always
// WRONG
@Service
class UserService {
  @Autowired private UserRepository repo;
}
// RIGHT
@Service
final class DefaultUserService implements UserService {
  private final UserRepository userRepository;
  DefaultUserService(UserRepository userRepository) {
    this.userRepository = checkNotNull(userRepository, "userRepository");
  }
}

// 3. Null return from a non-nullable method
// WRONG
public User findById(long id) {
  return userRepository.findById(id).orElse(null); // caller has no idea
}
// RIGHT
public Optional<User> findById(long id) { ... }
// OR throw a specific exception

// 4. Catching and swallowing exceptions
// WRONG
try {
  return userRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
} catch (Exception e) {
  return null; // what went wrong? nobody knows
}
// RIGHT
return userRepository.findById(id)
    .orElseThrow(() -> new UserNotFoundException(id));

// 5. Magic numbers
// WRONG
if (name.length() > 100) { ... }
// RIGHT
private static final int MAX_NAME_LENGTH = 100;
checkArgument(name.length() <= MAX_NAME_LENGTH,
    "name too long (%s chars, max %s): %s",
    name.length(), MAX_NAME_LENGTH, name);

// 6. Mutable public static state
// WRONG
public static List<String> ALLOWED_ROLES = new ArrayList<>();
// RIGHT
public static final ImmutableList<String> ALLOWED_ROLES =
    ImmutableList.of("ADMIN", "USER", "VIEWER");

// 7. Empty catch blocks
// WRONG
try {
  doSomething();
} catch (IOException e) {
  // TODO
}
// RIGHT — at minimum, log it; usually rethrow or wrap
try {
  doSomething();
} catch (IOException e) {
  throw new UncheckedIOException("failed to do something", e);
}
```

